      "rules": {
        "skeleton_rule": "opaque = alpha > 128 on the native-resolution 35 deg clockwise rotation. The cut skeleton is the opaque mask opened with a 1.5 mm radius: twigs and petals thinner than 3 mm of ink are not cut, so the gaps between branch/cluster groups are real openings (inlets and enclosed holes) through which the sky and moon show. Main component plus every detached component of at least 2 mm2 is kept; smaller specks are cut away.",
        "connector_rule": "each detached component is attached to the main skeleton along its own twig: the geodesic path inside the opaque mask from the fragment to the main component is buffered to 2.75 mm (the twig is printed inside the clear connector). Measured minimum feature of every connector >= 2.5 mm. The twig path is Gaussian-smoothed (sigma 2 px) and simplified (0.15 mm) before buffering so the laser path stays within the segment gate.",
        "opening_rule": "the cut body is skeleton + connectors, buffered 1.0 mm and closed 1.25 mm (sky slits under 2.5 mm filled). Enclosed holes at least 2.5 mm wide (erosion test) are kept as cut-out openings unless they would leave a neck under 2.5 mm or cross the riser; every other enclosed gap stays solid and is PRINTED with the back panel's blurred local colour (no clear acrylic fill inside the piece apart from the 1.0 mm rim, the connectors and the riser).",
        "print_rule": "the print is the original RGBA pixels inside the body 0.6 mm from every cut edge and opening (riser left clear); every enclosed gap - everything inside the piece that is not printed art, not the 1.0 mm clear band along a cut edge and not a clear connector halo - is printed with the back panel's tone sampled at the same scene position (extended sky raster Gaussian-blurred over 15 mm so waves and stars average into the gradient, plus the moon/cloud layer as one uniform pale colour through its own blurred mask), so the gaps read as the sky or moon behind them with no wave line, cloud edge or crater baked into the plate; the asset's semi-transparent fringes print only inside those gaps; nothing prints outside the body, so twigs and petals the cut skeleton dropped never print inside an opening and the outer rim stays clear.",
        "trunk_rule": "the tab axis is the lowest wood pixel of the rotated tree (wood = opaque pixel that is not red-dominant: r - max(g, b) < 45 or r < 110), i.e. the trunk base, exactly the V7 tab position (scene x ~131).",
        "doors": "each door island (alpha silhouette at 85 mm) buffered 1.0 mm, closed 1.25 mm, thin features widened to the 2.5 mm minimum and re-closed; enclosed lattice holes at least 2.5 mm wide after the rim are cut-out openings, every other lattice gap is printed with the back panel's blurred local colour. One 18 mm tab under the art centre, row 47."
